ont-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Below 0.05<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=84 valign=top style='width:63.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:16.65pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>ng\/mL<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=264 valign=top style='width:198.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:16.65pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Low\r\n  Risk for Sepsis: &lt; 0.5<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:12.6pt'>\r\n  <td width=235 valign=top style='width:176.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.6pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>(Serum,ECLIA)<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=138 valign=top style='width:103.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.6pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=84 valign=top style='width:63.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.6pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=264 valign=top style='width:198.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.6pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>High\r\n  Risk for Sepsis: &gt; 2<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=235 valign=top style='width:176.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=138 valign=top style='width:103.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=84 valign=top style='width:63.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=264 valign=top style='width:198.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Clinical\r\n  Correlation: 0.5-2<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=235 valign=top style='width:176.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=138 valign=top style='width:103.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=84 valign=top style='width:63.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=264 valign=top style='width:198.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>INTERPRETATION\r\n:<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>1.\u00a0 PCT is the\r\nprohormone of calcitonin secreted by different types of cells from numerous\r\norgans in response to <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 proinflammatory\r\nstimulation, particularly bacterial stimulation.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>2.\u00a0 Depending upon\r\nclinical background, PCT &gt; 0.1 can indicate clinically relevant bacterial\r\ninfection, requiring antibiotic\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 treatment.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>3.\u00a0 PCT is an important\r\nmarker enabling specific differentiation between bacterial infection and other\r\ncauses of\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 inflammatory\r\nreactions<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>4.\u00a0 Resorption of septic\r\ninfection is accompanied by decreases in PCT concentration which returns to\r\nnormal with half life\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 of 24 hours<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>5.\u00a0 In certain\r\nsituations (newborns, polytrauma, burns,major surgery, prolonged or severe\r\ncardiogenic shock etc) PCT\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 elevation may be\r\nindependent of any infectious aggression.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The return to\r\nnormal values is usually rapid<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>6.\u00a0 Viral infections,\r\nallergies, autoimmune diseases and graft rejection do not lead to significant\r\nincrease in PCT. Localized\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 bacterial\r\ninfections can lead to moderate increase in PCT levels.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"612.0pt 792.0pt","margin":"153.0pt 90.0pt 72.0pt 36.0pt"}}